//- 4:00 THE LINE OF PURPLES. The yes path starts here.

include ../partials/_horseshoe.pug

section#good.statement(data-timing="15")
  h2 Democracy works.
  p.aside (for now)
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Draft line. The room voted yes.

section.statement.horseshoe(data-timing="45")
  h2 Every wavelength you can see.
  h2.fragment(data-fragment-index="1") And a line your brain made up.
  +horseshoe
  aside.notes
    ul
      li The answer to the cliffhanger. The horseshoe is every wavelength you can see, 380 to 700 nanometres, in order.
      li Click: the straight edge. Its official name is the line of purples, and no single wavelength looks like anything on it.
      li Your brain sees violet at one end and red at the other, draws a line across the gap, and makes up colors to fill it.
      li Evidence: purple is the color your brain invents outright.
      li If challenged: the real CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram is lopsided, and this is its idea tidied into a horseshoe. The straight edge really is officially named the line of purples.
